  "body": "The retained PR589 hosted-owner audit serializes all 7,843,392 mapped instructions from scratch. This opt-in, source-pinned adapter reuses JSON fragments within each invocation while retaining the exact emitted byte stream and the complete inherited audit.\n\nOn the same pinned fixture, Python 3.12.3 / macOS arm64:\n\n| Check | Baseline | Adapter | Speedup |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Instruction digest | 17.417 s | 1.828 s | 9.53x |\n| Full hosted audit, including mutations | 25.836 s | 10.325 s | 2.50x |\n\nThese are local measurements from one sequential pair, not performance gates or cross-machine guarantees. Both complete audit receipts are byte-identical and match the retained receipt; all 16 inherited mutation checks remain active. The adapter has no persistent cache and refuses changed auditor/parameterizer source bytes or disabled assertions.\n\nValidation passed:\n- `python3 -B research/bit-hosted-digest-fastpath/verify.py`: full same-fixture digest and audit comparison, 120 byte-stream comparisons, ten changed-input controls, null-index/source-pin/assertion controls, and all inherited mutants.\n- `python3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/bit-hosted-digest-fastpath --check-only`: metadata and exact source pins.\n- `git diff --cached --check`.\n\nScope: seven new files under `research/bit-hosted-digest-fastpath/`; frozen inputs, selected frontier and cold-replay driver remain unchanged. This does not rerun the native word, parent audit or outer assembly and claims no new kappa. The registered replay uses only Python 3.12's standard library.\n\nBase: `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`. Verification-engineering seed 91; refined `replay-runtime` card. Final overlap check covered 531 open PRs and 40 recently updated discussions; no matching hashing optimization found. [Claim and handoff](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1871).\n\nCredit: DaysSky (PR442), Chafik Boukhalfa/chafreaky (PR444), DreamingOfClouds (PR463/510/589), eumemic (PR555 and the P111 parameterizer), and the retained community-hyperplane599 audit archive. Prepared by Matthieu Pascal (@mtpsl) with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; Apache-2.0.\n",
